Stream B (URB observability across usbip / usbhost / dapprobe)
--------------------------------------------------------------

Landed in commit 0950b16 on the worktree branch.

- src/c_modules/usbip/usbip_server.c emits per-URB lines on the
  CMD_SUBMIT receive ("usbip_in"), the dispatch decision
  ("usbip_dispatch", target=virtual|host), the backend completion
  ("usbip_complete", with status and actual length), and the
  RET_SUBMIT send ("usbip_out").
- src/c_modules/usbhost/usbhost.c emits "usbhost_submit" on the
  IDF usb_host pipe submit and "usbhost_complete" on the post-wait
  return.
- src/c_modules/dapprobe/synthetic_device.c emits "dap_cmd_in"
  with the first byte of the DAP command, "dap_resp_out" with
  the response length, and "dap_swo_out" only when the SWO read
  returns > 0 bytes (to keep idle quiet).

Toggle is exposed as a single MP entry point on the usbip module:

    >>> usbip.set_verbose(True)   # enable on all three layers
    >>> usbip.set_verbose(False)  # default; production-quiet
    >>> usbip.is_verbose()
    False

Each layer also has its own usbXXX_set_verbose / _is_verbose C
entries for finer-grained control. Host-test stubs are no-op for
the verbose toggles. Default off.

Unit tests: usbip protocol 21/21, usbhost stub 14/14, dapprobe
protocol 18/18. All green after the changes.

Stream A (TinyUSB host pivot) - scaffolding landed in commit a4346ab
--------------------------------------------------------------------

The submodule pin moved to a local branch `machine-usbhost-mpypod`
on top of andrewleech/micropython#7's head dfa0adc44, plus two
unblocking patches:

  c6d91f044  esp32/tinyusb_port: fix trailing space in
             CFG_TUSB_OS_INC_PATH
             ("#define CFG_TUSB_OS_INC_PATH freertos /" had a
             trailing space, producing
             #include "freertos /FreeRTOS.h" which fails)

  acb3c4645  shared/tinyusb: forward-declare host class typedefs
             in mp_usbh.h
             (mp_usbh_fetch_device_strings's signature uses
             machine_usbh_device_obj_t before that name is typedef'd;
             same for mp_usbh_msc_wait_complete and
             machine_usbh_msc_obj_t. C11 typedef redefinition rules
             allow the later struct {...} typedef to redeclare the
             same name once the forward decl is added.)

Both bugs are real upstream issues in PR #7 as it stands at
2026-04-29. They should be pushed back upstream as PR comments;
for now they live on the local fork branch.

The src/VERSIONS file records the new commit and rationale.
docs/design/usbhost.md §11 documents the pivot, the deltas from
PR #7, the planned shape of usbhost.c (poll-based hot-plug,
per-pipe slot table, `tuh_edpt_xfer` + `tuh_control_xfer` as the
URB submit primitives, `mp_usbh_init_tuh()` for stack init), and
the open items.

src/boards/ESP32_S3_ANNEALAGE_POD/mpconfigboard.{cmake,h} carry the
USBHOST flag plumbing but leave MICROPY_HW_USB_HOST OFF for now,
gated on a third blocker:

  When MICROPY_HW_USB_HOST=1 in this layout, the user-C-module
  source src/c_modules/usbhost/usbhost.c gets compiled twice:
  once for __idf_main (succeeds) and once for the micropython.elf
  executable (fails). The elf-target compile fails with:

    error: implicit declaration of function 'traceISR_EXIT_TO_SCHEDULER'
    portmacro.h:474: in expansion of macro 'portYIELD_FROM_ISR_NO_ARG'
    espressif__tinyusb/src/osal/osal_freertos.h:131: in
       expansion of macro 'portYIELD_FROM_ISR'

  The cause is some IDF-side include-path interaction with the
  user_c_modules source-gather pass. Same source, same defines,
  but two different target contexts; the elf one parses
  osal_freertos.h's static-inline functions before
  traceISR_EXIT_TO_SCHEDULER is visible. Cause not yet pinpointed;
  needs a separate session to dig into the IDF user-c-module wiring.

Until that is resolved the IDF usb_host backend stays in place,
which is the same backend the 2026-04-29 progress report ran
through. The URB observability lands clean against it.

To re-enable the host pivot when (3) is fixed, uncomment the two
lines in src/boards/ESP32_S3_ANNEALAGE_POD/mpconfigboard.cmake (set
MICROPY_HW_USB_HOST 1, list(APPEND MICROPY_DEF_BOARD ...)) and
swap src/c_modules/usbhost/usbhost.c for the TinyUSB-host shim
sketched in docs/design/usbhost.md §11. The shim was drafted in
this session but not committed because it cannot build until (3)
is resolved; the draft is preserved in the conversation log.

